[1920,1080]"><node index="0" text="" resource-id="" class="android.widget.ScrollView" package="com.fandomreader" content-desc="" checkable="false" checked="false" clickable="false" enabled="true" focusable="false" focused="false" scrollable="true" long-clickable="false" password="false" selected="false" bounds="[30,24][1890,1056]"><node index="0" text="Chapter Summary" resource-id="" class="android.widget.TextView" package="com.fandomreader" content-desc="" checkable="false" checked="false" clickable="false" enabled="true" focusable="false" focused="false" scrollable="false" long-clickable="false" password="false" selected="false" bounds="[30,24][278,73]" /><node index="1" text="Sorry about the reupload, I forgot to add a bit of grieving for Sirius. Because yes, he is dead." resource-id="" class="android.widget.TextView" package="com.fandomreader" content-desc="" checkable="false" checked="false" clickable="false" enabled="true" focusable="false" focused="false" scrollable="false" long-clickable="false" password="false" selected="false" bounds="[30,97][1286,146]" /><node index="2" text="And I also apologise to the people who took the time to leave comments on the original chapter. I honestly didn’t realise that deleting the chapter would delete them too XD." resource-id="" class="android.widget.TextView" package="com.fandomreader" content-desc="" checkable="false" checked="false" clickable="false" enabled="true" focusable="false" focused="false" scrollable="false" long-clickable="false" password="false" selected="false" bounds="[30,170][1890,268]" /><node index="3" text="Harry could not stop staring, and for once in his life, nobody was telling him it was rude." resource-id="" class="android.widget.TextView" package="com.fandomreader" content-desc="" checkable="false" checked="false" clickable="false" enabled="true" focusable="false" focused="false" scrollable="false" long-clickable="false" password="false" selected="false" bounds="[30,292][1236,341]" /><node index="4" text="He had spent the last weeks behind glass. That was the only way he could describe it – since the Ministry, there had been a pane between him and everyone else and people talked at him through it and their voices arrived late and slightly wrong. Nobody had managed to reach through it, and to be fair, nobody had tried very hard. The Order walked around him the way one walks around a cursed object – respectfully at a distance." resource-id="" class="android.widget.TextView" package="com.fandomreader" content-desc="" checkable="false" checked="false" clickable="false" enabled="true" focusable="false" focused="false" scrollable="false" long-clickable="false" password="false" selected="false" bounds="[30,365][1890,561]" /><node index="5" text="The ritual going wrong was the first thing in weeks that had happened to him instead of around him." resource-id="" class="android.widget.TextView" package="com.fandomreader" content-desc="" checkable="false" checked="false" clickable="false" enabled="true" focusable="false" focused="false" scrollable="false" long-clickable="false" password="false" selected="false" bounds="[30,585][1400,634]" /><node index="6" text="The man in the middle of the kitchen wore Harry's face." resource-id="" class="android.widget.TextView" package="com.fandomreader" content-desc="" checkable="false" checked="false" clickable="false" enabled="true" focusable="false" focused="false" scrollable="false" long-clickable="false" password="false" selected="false" bounds="[30,658][788,707]" /><node index="7" text="Older. Middle-aged, maybe, though it was hard to tell; there was grey at his temples and lines around his eyes that had nothing to do with laughing. Taller than Harry would ever be, he was fairly sure. No glasses. The scar was still there, faded to a thin pale line, half-hidden under his hair, and the eyes were Harry's eyes, his mother's eyes – except Harry had never seen them look like that in the mirror and sincerely hoped his own never would be. And he had grown a beard." resource-id="" class="android.widget.TextView" package="com.fandomreader" content-desc="" checkable="false" checked="false" clickable="false" enabled="true" focusable="false" focused="false" scrollable="false" long-clickable="false" password="false" selected="false" bounds="[30,731][1890,927]" /><node index="8" text="But it was his face, he could recognize himself, and that was somehow the least disturbing thing about him." resource-id="" class="android.widget.TextView" package="com.fandomreader" content-desc="" checkable="false" checked="false" clickable="false" enabled="true" focusable="false" focused="false" scrollable="false" long-clickable="false" password="false" selected="false" bounds="[30,951][1505,1000]" /><node index="9" text="Harry had spent a month in Grimmauld Place drowning in the Order's whispered fear of Voldemort, while Dumbledore was not meeting his eyes, with the constant grinding awareness of being fifteen and small and kept out of everything that mattered." resource-id="" class="android.widget.TextView" package="com.fandomreader" content-desc="" checkable="false" checked="false" clickable="false" enabled="true" focusable="false" focused="false" scrollable="false" long-clickable="false" password="false" selected="false" bounds="[30,1024][1890,1056]" /></node></node></node></node></node></node></node></hierarchy>